    "segments": [
      {
        "timestamp": "0:00",
        "text": "♪ Bass-heavy electronic music ♪ It's time for your final report."
      },
      {
        "timestamp": "0:05",
        "text": "♪ First, we covered how to improve battery consumption for your apps."
      },
      {
        "timestamp": "0:11",
        "text": "- Display is one of the major sources of power consumption."
      },
      {
        "timestamp": "0:15",
        "text": "- We learned how to make a Swift Server app alongside an iOS app in Xcode."
      },
      {
        "timestamp": "0:18",
        "text": "- Using Swift for building server components helps bridge this technology gap."
      },
      {
        "timestamp": "0:23",
        "text": "- Then Neil showed us how to match audio catalogs with video using ShazamKit."
      },
      {
        "timestamp": "0:27",
        "text": "- Now we have some important updates that streamline working with custom catalogs at scale."
      },
      {
        "timestamp": "0:32",
        "text": "- We discovered how to create multiple windows for our iPad apps."
      },
      {
        "timestamp": "0:35",
        "text": "- Here's an app I've built to keep track of the books I'm reading."
      },
      {
        "timestamp": "0:38",
        "text": "- And we closed out the week with a friendly device-to-device game of tic-tac-toe."
      },
      {
        "timestamp": "0:43",
        "text": "- And that's how easy it is to connect devices to Apple TV."
      },
      {
        "timestamp": "0:47",
        "text": "- Our training is complete, developers."
      },
      {
        "timestamp": "0:49",
        "text": "You're ready for your mission."
      },
      {
        "timestamp": "0:51",
        "text": "This message will self-destruct in 3... 2..."
      },
      {
        "timestamp": "0:54",
        "text": "Ah, just kidding! See you next year! ♪"
      }
    ]
  },
